;; read from readline (decoded by the encoding when one is given), the host tokenizes them (the compiler's mode
;; "tokenize:EXTRA", arbace.repr.python.astjson's tokenize-answer) and the iterator yields its tokens, as
;; tokenizeriter_next builds them: (type, string, (start line, start column), (end line, end column), line). The
;; error that ends the stream is raised after the tokens before it, the SyntaxError (IndentationError, TabError)
;; CPython's iterator raises. All the lines are read first: a readline with effects sees them read at once; what
;; readline raises, or a line of the wrong type, comes after the tokens of the lines before it, as the C iterator gives them.

